invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: the reduction modulo a prime returns without the wipe below its body, so
  the message's low and high words and r3 stay in the stack.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test requires no two words of a value the call held
  in the stack below it, and requires the stack equal under two secrets
  (docs/decisions.md 181).

--- old
    reduce_mod_prime(o, em, em_words, mod);
    rsa_sign64_wipe_below();
--- new
    reduce_mod_prime(o, em, em_words, mod);
